---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import inventory from '../../../../public/graphs/working/coverage-inventory.json';
const names = {'same-id-rewritten': 'Prior repair retained', 'restored-with-evidence-repair': 'Restored with evidence repair'};
const rows = inventory.originalQuestions;
---
<BaseLayout title="Graph coverage and migration" description="Analysis, repaired definitions and independent review status for all 588 original TENSOR questions in the 609-question working draft." canonicalPath="/graphs/coverage/">
  <ContentCard>
    <p class="section-kicker">Published knowledge → working definitions</p>
    <h2>All 588 original IDs are in the active draft.</h2>
    <p>The working draft has <strong>609 questions and 1,554 routes</strong>: all 588 original IDs plus 21 repair questions. The seven repaired entry paths remain intact. The published 588-question release and frozen institutional review package are unchanged.</p>
    <p>Each original now has an <strong>author-reviewed disposition</strong>. The 82 prior repairs retain their broader parameterized predicates; 506 originals return with explicit evidence criteria and repaired routes. Changes in meaning are recorded. A separate agent challenge review has repaired demonstrated route and evidence defects. External approval and equivalent investigative coverage remain unproved.</p>
    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/graphs/?graph=working&amp;renderer=3d">Explore the 609-question draft</a> <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/graphs/?graph=published">Preserved 588-question release</a></p>
    <h2>The full history stays visible</h2>
    <div class="coverage-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Questions</th><th>Change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Published release</td><td>588</td><td>Preserved source baseline</td></tr><tr><td>Earlier technical reduction</td><td>219</td><td>369 original IDs removed</td></tr><tr><td>Entry evidence repairs</td><td>184</td><td>49 originals detached; 14 questions added</td></tr><tr><td>Positive evidence repairs</td><td>103</td><td>88 originals detached; 7 questions added</td></tr><tr><td>Original-question restoration</td><td>609</td><td>506 originals revised and returned; prior repairs retained</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
    <p>Original unsupported edges were replaced, rather than reattached. Questions now separate matching records, provenance, operational comparators, independent corroboration, technical hypotheses, bounded scope, relations, technical sources or patterns, and comparable metric changes. Qualified endings preserve no/unknown answers and open questions without closing the investigation.</p>
    <p>The source contains <strong>479 distinct exact prompts</strong> and <strong>107 repeated-prompt groups involving 216 IDs</strong>. Repeated wording is disclosed; no consolidation or equivalence is assumed. Node count alone cannot establish coverage.</p>
    <h2>Seven-domain challenge review</h2>
    <p>Independent agent reviewers challenged the implementation and authored realistic normalized investigations across Identity, Host, Network, Cloud, Email, Application and File. The repairs remove <strong>278 unrelated affirmative topic jumps</strong>, preserve optional no/unknown answers, require actual directional dependency evidence and distinguish complete subject identities.</p>
    <p><strong>The earlier challenge passed 105 graph regression tests and 1,791 existing scenarios.</strong> The new profiles add 26 tests with counterexamples, bringing the combined graph suite to 131 tests; all 144 profile scenarios also pass. These tests use supplied observations and assessments; they do not authenticate production logs or constitute institutional approval. The seven base paths remain intact. General-question continuations explicitly preserve the source topic, subjects, time interval, hypothesis and prior answers.</p>
    <p><a href="/graphs/working/reviews/2026-10-12-independent-review/README.md">Read findings, repairs and test scope →</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/reviews/2026-10-12-independent-review/review.json" download>Exact review input pins</a></p>
    <h2>Event-context gaps now have explicit draft profiles</h2>
    <p><a href="/graphs/profiles/">Sixteen public event profiles across all seven domains</a> now cover credential/workload state, process-free host state, network configuration and sensor state, cloud data-plane access and resource state, mailbox rules/access and collaboration artifacts, background application/session state and autonomous actions, file deletion, historical lineage and unavailable-content metadata. Their 144 authored route scenarios include supported, refuted, unresolved and incomplete-evidence investigations.</p>
    <p>These are distinct profile-qualified definitions above the unchanged graph and schema. The ledger below retains the narrower unprofiled base contract; its limitations are historical applicability boundaries, not claims that the new profiles are unavailable. No invented subject identifiers or retroactive equivalence are implied. External approval, independent exchange and universal coverage remain open.</p>
    <h2>What external reviewers should challenge next</h2>
    <ol class="coverage-plan">
      <li><strong>Meaning and evidence in each domain.</strong> Review the source and revised proposition, facet, criteria and route rationale. Identify missing capabilities, unsupported inferences or useful consolidation.</li>
      <li><strong>Human and agent investigations with authorized evidence.</strong> Exercise supported, contradicted and unresolved paths. The 1,791 authored scenarios are regression evidence, not verified real-world efficacy.</li>
      <li><strong>Independent implementation and exchange.</strong> Preserve bound subjects/time and separate assessments using the pinned definitions and the separate Core candidate. Publish disagreements before promotion.</li>
    </ol>
    <p><a href="/docs/graph-coverage-roadmap.md">Review roadmap</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/reviews/2026-10-12-restoration/README.md">Restoration method and limits</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/reviews/2026-10-12-restoration/analysis.json" download>Complete per-ID analysis</a> · <a href="/graphs/working/coverage-inventory.json" download>Coverage ledger JSON</a></p>
    <h2>Original-question ledger</h2>
    <p><strong>{inventory.summary.authorReviewedDispositions} author-reviewed dispositions; {inventory.summary.approvedSemanticDispositions} independently approved.</strong> Source prompts, changed meaning, issues and target wording are available for every original. Historical removal stages remain in the downloaded ledger.</p>
    <div class="coverage-filters"><label>Search originals<input id="coverage-search" type="search" placeholder="ID, domain, topic, or prompt" /></label><label>Lineage<select id="coverage-status" aria-label="Lineage"><option value="">All stages</option>{Object.entries(names).map(([value,label])=><option value={value}>{label}</option>)}</select></label></div>
    <p id="coverage-count" aria-live="polite">588 original questions</p>
    <div class="coverage-table coverage-ledger" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="All original questions and their lineage">
      <table><thead><tr><th>Original question</th><th>Domain / stage</th><th>ID lineage</th><th>Semantic disposition</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map((row) => <tr id={row.sourceId} data-coverage-row data-status={row.lineageStatus}><td><a href={`/graphs/?graph=published&node=${row.sourceId}`}>{row.sourceId} · {row.sourceLabel}</a><details><summary>Original prompt</summary><p>{row.sourceText}</p></details></td><td>{row.category}<br /><small>{row.archetype}</small></td><td>{names[row.lineageStatus]}{row.activeId && <p><a href={`/graphs/?graph=working&node=${row.activeId}`}>Inspect working wording ↗</a></p>}</td><td><strong>{row.disposition === 'restore-with-evidence-repair' ? 'Revised and restored' : 'Prior evidence repair retained'}</strong><p>{row.sourceFacet}</p><details><summary>Meaning and identified issues</summary><p>{row.rationale}</p>{row.applicabilityLimitations?.map(limit => <p><strong>Applicability:</strong> {limit}</p>)}<ul>{row.issues.map(issue => <li>{issue}</li>)}</ul>{row.sourceDuplicateIds.length > 1 && <p>Repeated prompt IDs: {row.sourceDuplicateIds.join(', ')}. Equivalence is unproved.</p>}<p>{row.scenarioRefs.length} scenario references in the complete analysis.</p></details><small>Agent challenge completed · external domain approval pending</small></td></tr>)}</tbody></table>
    </div>
    <p><strong>{inventory.summary.absentOriginal} original IDs absent.</strong> This inventory does not assert equivalent meaning or exhaustive coverage.</p>
    <h2>Source pins</h2>
    <p>Published {inventory.published.version}: <code>{inventory.published.sha256}</code></p>
    <p>Working {inventory.working.version}: <code>{inventory.working.sha256}</code></p>
    <p><a href="/docs/legacy-migration.md">Preservation and migration method</a>. Reproduce the inventory with <code>python3 scripts/audit_graph_coverage.py --check</code> in a Framework checkout with full Git history. No schemas, released graph bytes, or investigation records are changed by this inventory.</p>
  </ContentCard>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  const search = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#coverage-search');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#coverage-status');
  const rows = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLTableRowElement>('[data-coverage-row]')];
  const apply = () => {
    let count = 0;
    for (const row of rows) {
      row.hidden = !row.textContent?.toLowerCase().includes(search?.value.trim().toLowerCase() || '') || Boolean(status?.value && row.dataset.status !== status.value);
      if (!row.hidden) count++;
    }
    const result = document.querySelector('#coverage-count');
    if (result) result.textContent = `${count} of 588 original questions`;
  };
  search?.addEventListener('input', apply); status?.addEventListener('change', apply);
</script>
<style>
  .coverage-table { overflow: auto; margin: 1rem 0; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .85rem; text-align: left; }
  tr[id] { scroll-margin-top: 6rem; }
  th, td { padding: .8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft); vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: var(--bg-card); }
  .coverage-ledger { max-height: 42rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .coverage-ledger th { position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1; }
  .coverage-ledger td:first-child { min-width: 15rem; max-width: 35rem; }
  details { margin-top: .4rem; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: .75rem; }
  .coverage-filters { display: flex; gap: 1rem; }
  .coverage-filters label { display: block; flex: 1; font-size: .8rem; }
  input, select { display: block; width: 100%; margin: .4rem 0; background: var(--bg-input); color: var(--text-primary); font: inherit; padding: .7rem; border: 1px solid var(--line-soft); }
  .coverage-plan li { margin: 1rem 0; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .coverage-filters { flex-direction: column; } }
</style>
